# Afenda feature server boundary

Feature packages centralize the server-only marker at their public `./server`
door:

```ts
import "@afenda/kernel/server";
```

Use that import only from `packages/features/<moduleId>/src/server.ts`.
Deep implementation files such as `data/*.server.ts`, `tools/*.server.ts`,
`workflows/*.server.ts`, `policies/*.server.ts`, and server components inherit
the boundary by being exported through the package server door.

Do not import `server-only` directly from `@afenda/feature-*` packages. The
`server-only` dependency belongs to `@afenda/kernel`; feature packages depend on
the public `@afenda/kernel/server` door instead.

Vitest package configs should use the shared config:

```ts
import { createVitestConfig } from "@afenda/config/vitest";

export default createVitestConfig("@afenda/feature-<moduleId>");
```

Avoid feature-local `server-only` stubs or aliases. If a test needs a deep
server implementation, import the implementation directly and mock its real
runtime dependencies instead of mocking `server-only`.
